    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG welcome to the market this exceptional top-floor luxury penthouse, offering the perfect blend of modern comfort and stylish living. Boasting two spacious double bedrooms, this stunning property extends to 70 sq. m. internally plus a remarkable 35 sq. m. southwest facing roof terrace, providing panoramic views of Dublin's iconic cityscape. From the soaring heights of Croke Park and the striking Poolbeg chimneys to the serene beauty of the Dublin Mountains, the outlook from this apartment is nothing short of breathtaking.\nThe apartment has been thoughtfully designed with quality finishes throughout, including a newly fitted handcrafted kitchen, contemporary bathrooms, and a spacious with additional storage. The highlight of this home is undoubtedly the private sun-drenched roof terrace, accessed from the living area and a separate south facing balcony off the bedrooms. Its enviable south-west aspect ensures an abundance of natural sunlight, making it the ideal space for outdoor dining, relaxing, or entertaining. No. 52 also benefits from two designated underground parking spaces and two storage units included in the sale.\nThe accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hallway with a convenient storage closet, a bright open-plan living/dining area with kitchen off it, two generous double bedrooms with the master featuring a modern en suite, and a recently upgraded family bathroom.\nOne is spoilt for choice with a host of local amenities and services on the doorstep of both Fairview and Drumcondra villages including an on-site Montessori in Fairview Close, local shops, churches, cafes, restaurants, pubs, sports and recreational facilities. Eastpoint business park is within a short stroll. Dublin city centre is 1.5 km from Fairview Close with Beaumont and Mater Hospitals, DCU and St Patrick's College all within 5 minutes driving distance as well as having easy access to the the M1, M50, Port Tunnel and Dublin Airport.\nThis is a rare opportunity to own a truly remarkable apartment in one of Dublin's most sought-after locations. Whether you're enjoying the tranquil surroundings of your terrace or taking in the vibrant energy of the city below, Apt. 52 at Fairview Close offers an unparalleled lifestyle."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nQuality laminate wood flooring, storage closet with plumbing for washing machine/dryer.\n\nLiving/Dining Room - \nQuality laminate wood flooring, large corner glazing with two doors out the the south facing balcony and also the south west facing sun terrace.\n\nKitchen - \nTiled floor and splashback, modern fully integrated white handleless kitchen with wooden countertops.\n\nBedroom 1 - \nQuality laminate wood flooring, built in wardrobes, door to the south facing balcony.\n\nEn Suite - \nFully tiled, WC, WHB, corner shower.\n\nBedroom 2 - \nQuality laminate wood flooring, built in wardrobes, door to the south facing balcony.\n\nBathroom - \nNewly fitted bathroom with tiled floor, bath surround and semi-tiled walls, WC, WHB, bath with overhead rainfall shower head, towel radiator.\n\nSun Terrace - \nSpacious south west facing sun terrace with composite decking and stunning views across the cityscape.\n\nFront Balcony - \nSouth facing balcony accessed from both bedrooms and living room, stunning views across the cityscape.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Gas fired central heating</li><li> Double glazed windows and external doors</li><li> Bespoke newly fitted kitchen and bathroom</li><li> A large south west facing sun terrace with stunning views</li><li> A south facing balcony</li><li> 2 Designated underground parking spaces</li><li> 2 Storage Units in the underground car park</li><li> Management fees 2,143 p.a. (2026)</ul>"
      },
